282	 * every id is checked against `cat` before it's used, so a stale or tampered
283	 * query string (an old link to a plan that's since been deactivated, say)
284	 * degrades to `seedOrder`'s normal defaults for whatever field didn't match,
285	 * never to a broken or half-filled order. Returns null when the URL carries
286	 * no recognised `product`, so the wizard opens on its ordinary empty first
